    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Peter Dorfman is the Tremere Pontifex overseeing the Mid-Atlantic (and formerly all United States) Tremere political affairs, a position that in almost any other city would make him prince outright &mdash; a fact that gnaws at him in Washington, where Marcus Vitel holds the throne. Embraced in 1700, Dorfman rules from the Octagon House Chantry, controls nearly a third of the city's political action committees, and carries numerous magical wards against Auspex, Dominate, and Presence at all times. He strongly suspects Vitel has Sabbat ties but refuses to act without absolute proof, and privately wages a covert war against the Technocracy's New World Order.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>You are in command of every situation. Never lose the initiative. Every pawn has its use, and there is always a need for more pawns. You have no superiors and few peers beyond Prince Vitel and Regent Meerlinda.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Simon Augustyn. Disciplines (as printed): Auspex 5, Dominate 5, Fortitude 3, Presence 5, Thaumaturgy 5 (Paths: Lure of Flames 5, Movement of the Mind 4, Weather Control 4, Spirit 3). Haven: several, primarily the Octagon House. Secrets: A. Convert Disciplines/Thaumaturgy Paths by adding owned power Items from the disciplines compendium at Storyteller discretion.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
